//! # Corner bracket — v0.1
//!
//! Outside-corner bracket for two 10 mm plywood panels. The original
//! parametric design is in [corner_bracket.scad](scad/corner_bracket.scad).
//! It has two captive-nut pockets accessible from the wood-facing surfaces
//! and two removable plugs that conceal the access windows after assembly.
//!
//! **This is a work in progress.** Test-fit the M4 fasteners, nuts, printed
//! clearances, plywood corner relief and printed-part strength before use.
//! All dimensions below are millimetres.
//!
//! ## Design walkthrough
//!
//! The separate [design.scad](scad/design.scad) uses the same CAD geometry.
//! Select a stage in its Customizer to inspect the construction interactively.
//! These six images are regenerated by CI directly from that source.
//!
//! ### 1. L-shaped side profile
//!
//! Start from a 2D L profile, round the inner corner and extrude to the
//! configured bracket width (`W = 20`). The arms are 40 mm long by default.
//!
//! ![Step 1: Extruded profile](design/01_profile.png)
//!
//! ### 2. Outer edge chamfers
//!
//! Apply a separate outer envelope to bevel the exposed side edges,
//! arm ends and outside corner; keep the plywood contact faces flat.
//!
//! ![Step 2: Outer chamfers](design/02_edge_chamfers.png)
//!
//! ### 3. Captive-nut pockets
//!
//! Subtract the two M4 clearance holes, hidden nut pockets, and access
//! windows. Nuts slide under the 3 mm retaining wall before fitting the
//! windows' closing plugs.
//!
//! ![Step 3: Nut pockets](design/03_nut_pockets.png)
//!
//! ### 4. Print-edge compensation
//!
//! Remove narrow 45-degree wedges along wood-facing edges to reduce
//! elephant-foot interference. The rounded inside corner must also be
//! matched by an appropriate radius on the plywood.
//!
//! ![Step 4: Final bracket](design/04_print_relief.png)
//!
//! ### 5. Access-window plugs
//!
//! Each access window receives one small plug. The printing layout places
//! the two plugs on their sides; each has a hooked tab for the retaining slot.
//!
//! ![Step 5: Two access plugs](design/05_access_plugs.png)
//!
//! ### 6. Installed preview
//!
//! Show the bracket outside the plywood corner, with both plugs fitted.
//! The plywood is a visual reference only, not part of the printable STL.
//!
//! ![Step 6: Installed bracket](design/06_installed.png)
//!
//! ***
//!
//! ## Printing and assembly
//!
//! 1. Print one bracket and one pair of access plugs, with each part on
//!    its flat side as arranged by the original designer.
//! 2. Check M4 nut fit in both pockets; insert nuts through the windows
//!    and slide them to the bolt holes.
//! 3. Engage each plug tab under its retaining lip and press the far end down.
//! 4. Fit the bracket on the outside corner of the plywood joint and
//!    fasten from the inside through the plywood. Confirm bolt lengths
//!    against real parts; nominal M4x16 is only a starting assumption.
//!
//! The CAD files below are the definitive geometry. The automatically
//! generated bill of materials includes the **printed bracket and one
//! two-plug set**. Plywood, bolts and nuts are not modeled BOM items.

include <NopSCADlib/core.scad>;
use <corner_bracket.scad>;

module corner_bracket_stl()
    stl("corner_bracket")
        bracket();

module access_plugs_stl()
    stl("access_plugs")
        plugs_print_pair();

//! Printed bracket and the pair of access-window plugs displayed side by
//! side. See the final design step above for their actual installed position.
module main_assembly()
    assembly("main") {
        stl_colour("SteelBlue") corner_bracket_stl();
        translate([58, 0, 0])
            stl_colour("Orange") access_plugs_stl();
    }

main_assembly();
